<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Required by RecognitionService's manifest contract, and NOT the empty stub it
  first appears to be. selectableAsDefault is the attribute that decides
  whether Penny survives a reboot as the assistant.

  Read out of AOSP's VoiceInteractionManagerService.initForUserNoTracing, which
  runs at every boot:

    - It reads Settings.Secure.VOICE_RECOGNITION_SERVICE first. If that is
      null, the whole "Current interactor/recognizer okay, done!" early return
      is skipped.
    - Execution then falls through to findAvailInteractor(userHandle, null),
      which will never auto-select a third-party app — AOSP: "We never want to
      allow third party services to be automatically selected."
    - So it reaches setCurInteractor(null, userHandle) and WIPES the assistant
      setting, every boot, silently.

  The only way to reach the early return is for the recognizer setting to point
  at a service that both resolves and reports isSelectableAsDefault(). That is
  this attribute. Without it, initForUser sets recognizerInfo = null with the
  comment "Unsetting the default and looking for another one", and Penny is
  evicted again.

  Measured on this device before it was added: the assistant role holder
  survived the reboot, but voice_interaction_service came back empty and
  dumpsys voiceinteraction said "(No active implementation)".
-->
<recognition-service
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:selectableAsDefault="true" />
